# {{projectName}}

Generated with [create-faster](https://github.com/plvo/create-faster) using the **Payload CMS (Cloudflare)** blueprint: a content-managed website on Cloudflare Workers. Editors publish pages and posts from the [Payload](https://payloadcms.com) admin at `/admin`, and the public site serves them from the edge as soon as they are published, without a deploy.

## Project Structure

A Turborepo with two Workers:

- `apps/web`: Next.js through OpenNext. The Payload admin (`/admin`), its REST API (`/api`) and the public site (`/`, `/posts`, a page for each slug, `sitemap.xml`, `robots.txt`), on `packages/ui`.
- `apps/cron`: a Hono Worker that backs up every table of the database to R2 each day.
- `packages/ui` and `packages/config`: the shadcn components and the shared TypeScript config.

The database is Cloudflare D1 and the media are in R2. Payload owns the schema and its migrations: there is no ORM package.

`robots.txt` disallows everything on `localhost` and on a `workers.dev` address, so the site is not indexed until it is served from a custom domain (set it as `NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL` for the build).

Running it needs nothing from Cloudflare, and nothing here reaches your account unless a command says it does. Deploying it needs the Workers Paid plan: the Free plan allows 10 ms of CPU per request and 50 D1 queries per invocation, which an admin request exceeds.

